; The stdlib extraction backend: the one backend this build can always
; construct, in its own library so a future backend with its own dependencies
; (Python's trafilatura extra) is a sibling stanza rather than a new import in
; [seekwright.fetch] itself. It depends on the fetch library for the backend
; contract ([Seekwright_fetch.Extractor.S]); nothing in the fetch library
; names it, so a fetcher holds an injected [Extractor.backend] and never a
; concrete module.
(library
 (name seekwright_fetch_stdlib)
 (public_name seekwright.fetch.stdlib)
 (libraries seekwright.fetch))
